# ZimaOS Setup Migration - Walkthrough

I have successfully organized the ZimaOS restoration and setup resources in a dedicated directory on your `D:` drive for a clean start.

## 📁 New Directory: `D:\OS`

The following files have been prepared and moved to `D:\OS`:

1. **[zimasetup.md](file:///D:/OS/zimasetup.md)**: Your primary setup guide containing the "One-Line Internet & SSH Fix".
2. **[cloudflare_token.txt](file:///D:/OS/cloudflare_token.txt)**: Your existing Cloudflare Tunnel token for easy restoration.
3. **[setup.sh](file:///D:/OS/setup.sh)**: The core ZimaOS/CasaOS installation script.
4. **[daemon.json](file:///D:/OS/daemon.json)**: Optimized Docker DNS configuration (`1.1.1.1`, `8.8.8.8`).

## 🚀 How to use [zimasetup.md](file:///D:/OS/zimasetup.md)

1. Open **[zimasetup.md](file:///D:/OS/zimasetup.md)**.
2. Replace `<USERNAME>` and `<PUBLIC_KEY>` with your values (The file includes a "Current Suggestion" based on our session).
3. Copy the command and paste it into the DeanOS terminal.

